{"ts":"2026-05-13T02:45:14.640Z","event":"bd_exec","request_id":"0ec8f196-bed3-4e2d-b4fd-c2d8bdc8780a","argv":["--json","create","Working directory: /Users/ricardo/Workshop/github/agent-pi\n\nThe shared helper now exists at `extensions/lib/commander/open-web-viewer.ts` — exports `openWebViewer(options, ctx)` with options { kind: 'static'|'interactive', title, reportType, mode?, content?, format?, url?, forceBrowser? } and returns { inCommander, reason?, action? }. Phase 1 is done.\n\n## Your job: route show_board through openWebViewer and add force_browser\n\n### File: `extensions/board-viewer.ts`\n\nRead the file fully first. Around lines 240-280 there is a `pi.registerTool` call for `show_board` whose execute calls `launchBoard(ctx, title)` and returns a text response. `launchBoard` (defined elsewhere in the same file or imported) currently calls `openBrowser(url)` directly.\n\nDo these edits:\n\n1. Add an optional `force_browser?: boolean` parameter to the tool's parameters schema (use the same Type system the file already uses — likely `Type.Optional(Type.Boolean({ description: '...' }))`). Description should match show_plan's wording: 'Bypass Commander and open the local browser viewer directly. Useful for testing browser fallback.'\n\n2. Locate the `openBrowser(url)` call inside the show_board codepath (likely inside `launchBoard` or a helper it calls). Replace it with a call to `openWebViewer({ kind: 'interactive', url, title, reportType: 'generic', forceBrowser: params.force_browser }, ctx)`. \n\n3. If `launchBoard` does not currently receive `force_browser` or `ctx`, thread them through. Keep the function's return value (the URL string) intact — callers depend on it.\n\n4. Import { openWebViewer } from './lib/commander/open-web-viewer' at the top of the file (match the existing import style — `.ts` extension or not, whatever the file uses).\n\n5. Remove the direct `openBrowser` import if it becomes unused.\n\n### Verify\n\n- Run `npx vitest run extensions/__tests__/open-web-viewer.test.ts` — must still pass\n- Run `npx vitest run extensions/__tests__/` for any board-related test — must still pass\n- Run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` if a tsconfig exists, or `npx tsc --noEmit extensions/board-viewer.ts` and report only NEW errors you introduced (the codebase has pre-existing tsc errors — ignore those)\n\n### Deliver\n\n- Exact diff summary (lines changed)\n- Test results\n- Any deviation\n\nDo NOT modify any other file in this task. Be surgical.","-d","Working directory: /Users/ricardo/Workshop/github/agent-pi\n\nThe shared helper now exists at `extensions/lib/commander/open-web-viewer.ts` — exports `openWebViewer(options, ctx)` with options { kind: 'static'|'interactive', title, reportType, mode?, content?, format?, url?, forceBrowser? } and returns { inCommander, reason?, action? }. Phase 1 is done.\n\n## Your job: route show_board through openWebViewer and add force_browser\n\n### File: `extensions/board-viewer.ts`\n\nRead the file fully first. Around lines 240-280 there is a `pi.registerTool` call for `show_board` whose execute calls `launchBoard(ctx, title)` and returns a text response. `launchBoard` (defined elsewhere in the same file or imported) currently calls `openBrowser(url)` directly.\n\nDo these edits:\n\n1. Add an optional `force_browser?: boolean` parameter to the tool's parameters schema (use the same Type system the file already uses — likely `Type.Optional(Type.Boolean({ description: '...' }))`). Description should match show_plan's wording: 'Bypass Commander and open the local browser viewer directly. Useful for testing browser fallback.'\n\n2. Locate the `openBrowser(url)` call inside the show_board codepath (likely inside `launchBoard` or a helper it calls). Replace it with a call to `openWebViewer({ kind: 'interactive', url, title, reportType: 'generic', forceBrowser: params.force_browser }, ctx)`. \n\n3. If `launchBoard` does not currently receive `force_browser` or `ctx`, thread them through. Keep the function's return value (the URL string) intact — callers depend on it.\n\n4. Import { openWebViewer } from './lib/commander/open-web-viewer' at the top of the file (match the existing import style — `.ts` extension or not, whatever the file uses).\n\n5. Remove the direct `openBrowser` import if it becomes unused.\n\n### Verify\n\n- Run `npx vitest run extensions/__tests__/open-web-viewer.test.ts` — must still pass\n- Run `npx vitest run extensions/__tests__/` for any board-related test — must still pass\n- Run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` if a tsconfig exists, or `npx tsc --noEmit extensions/board-viewer.ts` and report only NEW errors you introduced (the codebase has pre-existing tsc errors — ignore those)\n\n### Deliver\n\n- Exact diff summary (lines changed)\n- Test results\n- Any deviation\n\nDo NOT modify any other file in this task. Be surgical.","-p","4","-t","task","--label","cmd-parent:agent-pi-2gt"],"cwd":"/Users/ricardo/Workshop/GitHub/agent-pi","exec_ms":380,"status":1,"ok":false}
